# Responsive: mobile · desktop · TV

Build UI that works on touch phones, mouse desktops, and large TV/lean-back screens. Never ship hover-only interactions.

## Breakpoints (prefer these)

- **Mobile**: `max-width: 480px` (single column) and `max-width: 800px` / `900px` (stacked / sheet UI)
- **Desktop**: `min-width: 901px` with fine pointer
- **Large / TV**: `min-width: 1600px` (and optionally `min-width: 1920px`) — larger type, wider popovers, more breathing room; avoid tiny hit targets

Detect touch/narrow UI in TS with `(pointer: coarse)` **or** `max-width: 900px`, not hover alone.

## Interaction rules

- Every hover affordance needs a **tap/click** equivalent (toggle, button, or link).
- Overlays/popovers on touch or ≤900px: **fixed bottom sheet**, dimmed **backdrop**, visible **close**, **Escape**, and **body scroll lock** while open.
- Hide close/backdrop only when `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) and (min-width: 901px)`.
- Hit targets ≥ 44×44px on touch. Prefer `@media (pointer: coarse)` for larger taps.
- Prefer `clamp()` for type/spacing so TV and mobile scale without separate copy blocks.

## Layout

- Mobile-first grids; collapse multi-column stats/cards before they crush.
- No horizontal page scroll; popovers must not clip off-screen — use sheets on small/touch.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` for GSAP/CSS motion.
- TV: keep focus/contrast high; don’t rely on hover glow as the only state.

## Example

```typescript
// ✅ touch + narrow share one mode
readonly isTouchUi = signal(
  matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches || matchMedia('(max-width: 900px)').matches
);
// open on mouseenter only when !isTouchUi(); always support click toggle + Escape
```

```scss
// ✅ sheet on touch/narrow; anchored popover on desktop fine pointer
@media (max-width: 900px), (pointer: coarse) {
  .pop { position: fixed; inset: auto 0.75rem 0.75rem; max-height: 72vh; overflow: auto; }
}
```
